---
import '../styles/site.css';

const arxivUrl = 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.29907';
const githubUrl = 'https://github.com/dishenliu2004-hub/UnderGrasp';

const trials = [
  ['Single object', 'single', 'Grasping individual test objects with the underactuated gripper.'],
  ['Cluttered scene', 'clutter', 'Grasping a target among neighboring objects.'],
  ['Method comparison', 'comparison', 'Compare the execution of grasp candidates across methods.'],
  ['Transport after grasping', 'transport', 'Post-grasp transport with AnyGrasp, fixed-depth insertion, and UnderGrasp.']
];
const results = [
  ['AnyGrasp', '55%', '12%'], ['AnyGrasp + 40 mm insertion', '52%', '35%'],
  ['AnyGrasp + UnderGrasp', '82%', '55%'], ['GraspNet', '42%', '8%'],
  ['GraspNet + UnderGrasp', '65%', '36%']
];
const citation = `@misc{song2026undergrasp,
  title = {UnderGrasp: Envelopment-Oriented Grasp Refinement for an Underactuated Gripper},
  author = {Song, Zhiwen and Liu, Ruidi and Jia, Guanglu and Chen, Zuowei and Wen, Hao and Shi, Qing},
  year = {2026}
}`;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>UnderGrasp | Envelopment-Oriented Grasp Refinement</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Real-robot demonstrations, method and experimental results for UnderGrasp, a grasp refinement framework for an underactuated gripper." />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:," />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="hero wrap" id="overview">
        <div class="intro">
          <h1><span>UnderGrasp</span>Envelopment-Oriented Grasp Refinement for an Underactuated Gripper</h1>
          <p class="authors">Zhiwen Song<sup>1†</sup>, Ruidi Liu<sup>2†</sup>, Guanglu Jia<sup>1*</sup>, Zuowei Chen<sup>1</sup>, Hao Wen<sup>1</sup> and Qing Shi<sup>1</sup></p>
          <p class="aff"><sup>1</sup> Beijing Institute of Technology &nbsp; <sup>2</sup> Beijing University of Technology</p>
          <small>† Equal contribution · * Corresponding author</small>
          <div class="actions">
            {arxivUrl
              ? <a href={arxivUrl}>arXiv</a>
              : <button type="button" disabled>arXiv</button>}
            <a href={githubUrl}>Code</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="feature"><video controls playsinline muted preload="none" poster="./media/envelopment.jpg" src="./media/envelopment.mp4" aria-label="Grasping demonstration"></video><figcaption>Parallel and enveloping grasps under the same external disturbance.</figcaption></figure>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section" id="abstract">
        <h2>Abstract</h2>
        <p class="lead">Underactuated grippers can form enveloping grasps through passive compliance, while the terminal pose and single width predicted by generic grasp generators do not fully capture the approach–closure process. Conventional collision filtering also struggles to distinguish harmful interference from acceptable contact. We present UnderGrasp, a post-hoc grasp refinement and evaluation framework for an underactuated gripper that reuses grasp candidates and quality priors from a frozen generator. The model jointly encodes the target, local environment, support surface, and approach-path geometry to propose diverse combinations of insertion depth, pre-grasp width, and target closing width for each candidate. These actions are ranked by combining separately predicted envelopment and interaction quality with upstream priors, balancing grasp feasibility, envelopment, and scene disturbance rather than rejecting all environmental contact. The back end is trained solely on configuration and interaction labels generated by gripper-specific simulations, without real-robot grasp labels. Real-robot experiments with an underactuated gripper show that UnderGrasp improves the overall success rate (SR) and the envelopment rate among successful grasps (ER) from 0.55/0.12 to 0.82/0.55 with AnyGrasp, and from 0.42/0.08 to 0.65/0.36 with GraspNet. In contrast, increasing the fixed insertion depth to 40 mm improves ER to 0.35 but reduces SR to 0.52, supporting the value of adaptive refinement. For trials involving target or environmental contact during approach, the conditional success rates increase from 0.36 to 0.89 and from 0.25 to 0.86, respectively, demonstrating more reliable execution under contact.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section" id="method">
        <h2>From pose to grasp execution</h2>
        <div class="method-intro">
          <p>For each grasp candidate, UnderGrasp proposes a set of actions with different combinations of insertion depth, pre-grasp width, and target closing width. Each action receives a score that combines its predicted envelopment and interaction qualities with the generator’s score for the original candidate. The gripper executes the highest-scoring action.</p>
          <figure>
            <a href="./media/method.png" aria-label="View the full-resolution network architecture"><img loading="lazy" src="./media/method.png" alt="Four candidate-centered point clouds feed the proposal and evaluation heads, which rank actions alongside the frozen generator." /></a>
            <figcaption><a href="./media/method.png">View full architecture</a></figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="method-videos">
            <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./media/pipeline.jpg" src="./media/pipeline.mp4" aria-label="UnderGrasp pipeline"></video><figcaption>Refinement and evaluation pipeline</figcaption></figure>
            <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./media/pose.jpg" src="./media/pose.mp4" aria-label="Grasp pose examples"></video><figcaption>Grasp pose refinement</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section simulation" id="simulation">
        <div>
          <h2>Learning envelopment in simulation</h2>
          <p>MuJoCo provides finger configurations, scene changes and capture outcomes from 66,560 simulated actions on 12 training objects.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="./media/training.png" aria-label="View full-size simulation data and experimental objects"><img loading="lazy" src="./media/training.png" alt="Simulation data collection, training objects and unseen real-world test objects grouped by geometry." /></a>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section" id="experiments"><h2>Real-robot grasping</h2>
        <div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose an experiment">{trials.map(([label, slug, caption], i) => <button type="button" aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} data-clip={slug} data-caption={caption}>{label}</button>)}</div>
        <div aria-live="polite">
          <p class="lead" id="grasp-protocol">We evaluated each method on 10 objects excluded from UnderGrasp’s back-end training. Each object was tested three times in clean scenes and three times in cluttered scenes, for a total of 60 trials per method. A trial was successful if the robot grasped the target, returned to its initial pose, and held the object for three seconds without dropping it.</p>
          <p class="lead" id="transport-protocol" hidden>After a successful initial grasp, the robot transported a watering can filled with 500 mL of water at 40%, 70%, or 100% of its maximum speed. For each method, we counted successful transports in five trials at each speed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="result-grid">
            <figure><video id="trial" controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./media/single.jpg" src="./media/single.mp4" aria-label="Single object"></video><figcaption id="trial-caption" aria-live="polite">{trials[0][2]}</figcaption></figure>
          <div id="grasp-results"><h3>Overall performance</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>SR</th><th>ER</th></tr></thead><tbody>{results.map(([label,sr,er]) => <tr class:list={[{ours:label.includes('UnderGrasp')}]}><th scope="row">{label}</th><td>{sr}</td><td>{er}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="note">SR is the fraction of all trials that succeed. ER is the fraction of successful grasps that envelop the object.</p></div>
          <figure id="transport-results" hidden>
            <h3>Transport performance</h3>
            <img loading="lazy" src="./media/transport-results.png" alt="At 40%, 70% and 100% speed, successful runs out of five were 5, 4, 3 with UnderGrasp, 4, 3, 2 with fixed insertion, and 1, 0, 0 with AnyGrasp." />
            <figcaption>Successful transports in five trials per method at each speed.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section divider" id="citation"><h2>Citation</h2><pre><code id="bibtex">{citation}</code></pre><button id="copy" type="button" aria-live="polite">Copy BibTeX</button></section>
    </main>
    <footer><div class="wrap"><b>UnderGrasp</b><a href="#overview">Back to top</a></div></footer>
    <script>
      const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy')!;
      copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.querySelector('#bibtex')!.textContent || '');
          copy.textContent = 'Copied';
        } catch {
          copy.textContent = 'Select the citation above to copy';
        }
      });
      const player = document.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>('#trial')!;
      const graspResults = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#grasp-results')!;
      const transportResults = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#transport-results')!;
      const graspProtocol = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#grasp-protocol')!;
      const transportProtocol = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#transport-protocol')!;
      const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-clip]');
      for (const button of buttons) {
        button.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (button.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true') return;
          buttons.forEach(item => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
          const transport = button.dataset.clip === 'transport';
          graspProtocol.hidden = transport;
          transportProtocol.hidden = !transport;
          graspResults.hidden = transport;
          transportResults.hidden = !transport;
          player.poster = './media/' + button.dataset.clip + '.jpg';
          player.src = './media/' + button.dataset.clip + '.mp4';
          player.setAttribute('aria-label', button.textContent || 'Experiment');
          document.querySelector('#trial-caption')!.textContent = button.dataset.caption || '';
          player.play().catch(() => {});
        });
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
